Module muster "The Long Muster's Road" {
  // ── Eleven hundred and four years, as the Annals keep them ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The valley's history goes beyond the company's visit: three years the Annals mark in red, each a quarrel that
  // made the valley what it is. They are told by the Archivist, one topic apiece, once he trusts the company; and
  // each leaves a custom in the valley that can be seen without being told.
  Relation annalsOpen(group).
  Discovery second_wife_known "In the year 212 the Prefect Aulus took a second wife from the Hearth while the first, an Eagle's daughter, still lived; the valley has eaten at two tables since.".
  Discovery plague_winter_known "In the year 640 a plague killed a third of the valley in a winter; the lot was drawn, and the courier died at the Sending gate, and since then the Sending goes out with a white cord at its wrist.".
  Discovery schism_known "In the year 871 the Eagles proposed to send the standard itself north with the Sending, to be put into the Emperor's hand. In the night the gold wings were taken, and a brass eagle in a skin of bronze stood on the pole by morning. The Eagles said the Hearth had stolen them. A man was killed. The quarrel is two hundred and thirty-three years old.".
  Discovery two_sendings_known "In the year 1002 the valley sent two couriers, one by the Eagles and one in secret by the Hearth; neither came home; neither is in the Annals but in the margin, as: both.".

  Topic moll_annals with fenwarden "Ask the Archivist to open the Annals" when admitted(party) and not annalsOpen(party) and knows(actor, rufus_1) {
    Says "He lifts down a book that takes both arms. 'Eleven hundred and four years, mostly weather and who was Prefect. Four years are written in red.' He keeps his hand on the cover. 'I show the red ones to someone who has sworn on the shrine lamp not to use them against the valley, and who has brought me one thing I do not already know. You have brought Rufus. Swear.'".
    On discuss { Assert annalsOpen(party). }
  }
  Topic moll_wife with fenwarden "Ask the Archivist about the year of the second wife" when annalsOpen(party) and mollSwore(party) {
    Says "'The year two hundred and twelve,' says Fenwarden. 'The Prefect Aulus was an Eagle, and his wife an Eagle's daughter, and he thought she was barren. So he took a second wife from the Hearth, a farmer's girl with no schooling. And the first wife lived. The valley has eaten at two tables since.' He taps the line. 'The Prefect eats at the Eagles' table one day and the Hearth's the next. Nobody remembers why. Nobody has broken it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, second_wife_known). }
  }
  Topic moll_plague with fenwarden "Ask the Archivist about the plague winter" when annalsOpen(party) and mollSwore(party) {
    Says "'Six hundred and forty. One in three.' Fenwarden turns a page. 'The Sending was due and the lot fell on a girl of nineteen, and she walked out of the gate with the pouch and fell down dead on the path with her white cord on. Nobody touched her for a day. Since then the courier wears a white cord. It is not for mourning. It is so the valley knows whose turn it was, if there is no one left to say.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, plague_winter_known). }
  }
  Topic moll_schism with fenwarden "Ask the Archivist about the Schism of the Standard" when annalsOpen(party) and mollSwore(party) {
    Says "'Eight hundred and seventy-one,' says Fenwarden, in the voice of a man reading a charge sheet. 'A young Aquilifer proposed in the evening call that the standard be carried north with the Sending and put into the Emperor's hand. The Eagles roared. The Hearth said nothing. In the night the wings were taken. In the morning a brass eagle in a skin of bronze stood on the pole, and the Aquilifer, who loved the old bird more than his mother, hanged himself in the shrine.' He shuts the book. 'Three days of fighting in the forum. A man killed. The Eagles have said since that the Hearth stole the gold. The Hearth has said nothing at all.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, schism_known). }
  }
  Topic moll_two with fenwarden "Ask the Archivist about the year of two Sendings" when annalsOpen(party) and knows(actor, schism_known) {
    Says "'One thousand and two. The Annals say the Eagles' courier went, as ever. In the margin, in a hand I do not know, one word: BOTH. A courier from the Hearth, by the goat path, in the night.' He taps it. 'Neither came home. I have looked for the second name for thirty years.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, two_sendings_known). }
  }
  Observe beam_scene at archive when true "A roof-beam of black cedar runs the length of the Archive, and cut along its underside, in small even notches grouped in fives, is a tally that goes from the north wall to the south. The last groups are fresh and pale. There are, you count idly, a great many.".
  Observe two_tables at praetorium_hall when knows(party, second_wife_known) "Two tables stand in the hall's end, set for a meal, one with red cloth and one with brown. The Prefect, you notice, is at the red one today.".
  Observe white_cord at gate as sign when knows(party, plague_winter_known) "On a peg inside the gate hangs a white cord, worn to a grey rope, waiting for the spring.".
  Observe schism_scar at forum when knows(party, schism_known) "On the paving at the foot of the standard's pole there is a darker patch, worn smooth. Nobody walks on it. The children step round it.".
}
